                  CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware
designers and to provide a legal tool which supports the
freedom to use, study, modify, share and distribute hardware designs and
products based on those designs. Version 2 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence
comes in three variants: CERN-OHL-P (permissive); and two reciprocal
licences: CERN-OHL-W (weakly reciprocal) and this licence, CERN-OHL-S
(strongly reciprocal).

The reciprocal variants are designed to be compatible with one another and
with other reciprocal licences whilst imposing conditions to ensure that the
original source may be shared widely. This is achieved through a mechanism
which ensures that all modifications and derivatives of the original source
are made available under the same licence.

CERN-OHL-S is the most restrictive of the three variants. Under CERN-OHL-S,
if You make modifications to the source files (for example, KiCad schematic
or layout files) and distribute or make products using those modifications,
You must make those modified source files available under CERN-OHL-S.

Definitions

1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S.

1.2 'Compatible Licence' means

     a) any earlier version of the CERN Open Hardware licence, or

     b) any version of the CERN-OHL-S or the CERN-OHL-W or,

     c) any licence which permits You to treat the Source to which it applies
        as licenced under CERN-OHL-S provided that on each occasion You must
        also comply with the conditions in this Licence.

1.3 'Source' means information such as design materials or digital code which
    can be applied to Make or test a Product or to prepare a Product for use,
    distribution or sale, regardless of its medium or how it is expressed. It
    may include Notices.

1.4 'Covered Source' means Source that is explicitly made available under
    this Licence.

1.5 'Product' means any device, component, work or physical object, whether
    in finished or intermediate form, arising from the use, application or
    processing of Covered Source.

1.6 'Make' means to create or configure something, whether by manufacture,
    assembly, compiling, loading or applying Covered Source or another Product
    or otherwise.

1.7 'Available Component' means any part, sub-assembly, library or code which:

     a) is licensed under terms that do not impose reciprocal licensing
        obligations on the Covered Source under which it is included; or

     b) is a standard part, tool, library or code, which is widely available
        and which is neither specific nor unique to the Covered Source in which
        it is incorporated.

1.8 'External Material' means anything (including Source) which:

     a) is only combined with Covered Source in a way that interfaces with
        it using a documented interface specification; and

     b) is not a derivative of or does not include Covered Source, or, if it
        does, it is solely to the extent necessary to facilitate such
        interfacing.

1.9 'Notices' means copyright, acknowledgement and trademark notices,
    references to the location of any Notices, modification logs and all
    notices that refer to this Licence and to the disclaimer of warranties
    that are included in the Covered Source.

1.10 'Licensee' or 'You' means any person exercising rights under this
     Licence.

1.11 'Licensor' means any person who creates or modifies Covered Source. A
     person may be a Licensee and a Licensor at the same time.

1.12 'Revision' means any modification to Covered Source resulting in a new
     version of it with a version number or date different from the previous.

1.13 'Source Location' means a location where a Licensor has placed Covered
     Source, and which that Licensor reasonably believes will remain easily
     accessible for at least three years for anyone to obtain a digital copy.

1.14 'Notice' means a written communication in the form of a notice,
     acknowledgement, disclaimer or legend placed in the documentation or
     on a physical product.

Applicability

This Licence governs the use, copying, modification, distribution of Covered
Source (including the compiled, mapped or object form of a Source and any
modifications of it), and the Making of Products. By exercising any right
granted under this Licence, You irrevocably accept these terms and conditions.

This Licence is granted by the Licensor directly to You, and shall apply
worldwide and without limitation in time.

You agree that hardware is inherently different from software in that a
design file may be easily reproducible but its reproduction in physical form,
without changes, is not always possible. This Licence recognises that what
is important is not the physical form of a Product, but the design that
allows it to be Made.

Conditions

3.1 - Notices

You must ensure that every copy of the Covered Source You distribute is
accompanied by a copy of the Notices associated with that version of the
Covered Source. You must also ensure that the Covered Source Location is
included in the Notices where practicable.

If You create a Revision and make it available, You must add a Revision
Notice to the Notices.

3.2 - Applying the Licence to Your Covered Source

You may not impose any further restrictions on the exercise of the rights
granted or affirmed under this Licence. Licences granted to anyone under
this Licence shall not impose any conditions additional to those in this
Licence. You are not required to accept this Licence in order to receive or
run a copy of the Covered Source.

However, by exercising any of the rights granted under this Licence to
receive, copy, modify or distribute a copy of the Covered Source or to Make
a Product, You indicate your acceptance of this Licence and all its terms and
conditions.

3.3 - Reciprocal licensing conditions for Covered Source

If You distribute Covered Source (including in compiled, object or other
form), You must:

     a) retain all Notices;

     b) include a copy of this Licence with the Covered Source; and

     c) make the Covered Source (including any modifications You have made to
        it, in accordance with section 3.4) available under this Licence,
        including by providing its Source Location.

3.4 - Reciprocal licensing conditions for Products

If You Make a Product which in whole or in part is based on Covered Source,
You must ensure that anyone who receives the Product can exercise the rights
granted by this Licence with respect to the Covered Source incorporated in
the Product, including but not limited to the right to obtain a copy of
that Covered Source, by either:

     a) including a copy of the Covered Source, and the Notices (if any),
        with the Product, or accompanying materials provided with the Product;
        or

     b) providing the Source Location of the Covered Source, and the Notices
        (if any), in the Product documentation or on the labelling of the
        Product, or on a website or other means of access, such that anyone
        acquiring the Product can readily obtain a copy of the Covered Source.

3.5 - Notices and Source Location

The Source Location must be included in any Notices required under section
3.1 and on any label, documentation, or packaging provided with the Product.
Where you place Notices on the Product, Source Location must be clearly
legible and in a form that can reasonably be expected to be read by a person
acquiring the Product.

3.6 - Compiled Source and Object code

Where Covered Source is not supplied in a form normally used for making
modifications, You must also make it available in a form normally used for
making modifications (for example, the KiCad schematic and PCB layout files).

Warranties and Liability

4.1 - DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES

COVERED SOURCE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND ANY EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES,
INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
SATISFACTORY QUALITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT
OF THIRD PARTY INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY RIGHTS ARE DISCLAIMED. IN NO EVENT
SHALL ANY LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
EXEMPLARY, OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO,
PROCUREMENT OF SUBSTITUTE GOODS OR SERVICES; LOSS OF USE, DATA, OR PROFITS;
OR BUSINESS INTERRUPTION) HOWEVER CAUSED AND ON ANY THEORY OF LIABILITY,
WHETHER IN CONTRACT, STRICT LIABILITY, OR TORT (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR
OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS COVERED SOURCE, EVEN
IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.

4.2 - Liability

Nothing in this Licence shall exclude or limit liability for:

     a) death or personal injury caused by gross negligence or wilful
        misconduct;

     b) fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation;

     c) any other liability that cannot be excluded or limited by applicable
        law.

5.  Termination

5.1 If You breach any of the terms of this Licence, Your rights under this
    Licence will terminate automatically and immediately. Any licences You
    have granted to others will, however, remain valid for as long as those
    persons comply with the terms of those licences.

5.2 You may terminate this Licence for any version of the Covered Source by
    notifying the Licensor (or its successors), but only if:

     a) You have no obligation to provide the Covered Source of that version
        to anyone at the time of termination; and

     b) the Licensor agrees in writing to the termination.

Licence Compatibility

If You receive Covered Source under a Compatible Licence, You may, at Your
option, treat the Covered Source as being made available under this Licence.
For the avoidance of doubt, the fact that another licence is listed as
Compatible with this Licence does not mean that this Licence is compatible
with that other licence.

